Z||000000||frontal lobe||10-29-2001||10:31 PM||||I was bored one night while on the internet, and I had seen warez mentioned on the windows xp thread, so I thought I would check the site out.  I clicked on the highest rated download site and all of a sudden I have porno sites popping up one right after another without even clicking on a thing.  Fortunately on the "turn off the internet" thread, I had learned to use alt f4 so I could shut them as soon as they started to pop up, but I was mad.<P>Today I get on the internet and hit the internet explorer button and it takes me to warez again!  And multiple sites start opening up, some porno and some not.  I close all those.  I go to the tools, check out the default site, AND WAREZ HAD SOMEHOW PUT ITSELF IN THERE!  What is going on?  How did they do that?<P>I had to go into the temporary internet files and delete everything, only it wouldn't let me delete something called creative 1.  It seemed to keep replicating itself in other temporary internet files.  I kept trying and finally got everything deleted, and got control of my computer back.  But I am really ticked.<P>Does anyone know anything about this site, and how they can do all that?  I'd love to know where the person that owns it is, and if it was close enough to where I live, I would try to make a personal visit.||||reg||1
Z||000001||btoth||10-29-2001||10:50 PM||||LOL<P>You don't go to warez sites very often do you?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> J/K<P><BR>What site was it?  Top 50/100??  It sounds like you clicked one of those buttons asking if you wanted to make the page your homepage.<P>I don't believe there's anything you could do about it.  Pop-up windows are not illegal, and the pop-up sites are the warez site's sponsers most likely.  Just don't go to them.||||reg||1
