Z||000010||SteveJ||10-30-2001||08:12 AM||||Go to  <A HREF="http://www.popupstopper.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.popupstopper.net/</A> <P>and get their popup stopper 2.4. It's free and can prevent popup windows. You can even start it after you have entered a site where they are doing that. It can be turned on and off while running too.<BR>Cookies can be turned off in the browser with little effect. The only time I have them on is when I register on a new board. Cookies have become advertising vehicles. Some are spyware. Thanks to btoth we know of adware 5.62 at<BR> <A HREF="http://www.lavasoftusa.com" TARGET=_blank>www.lavasoftusa.com</A> <P>This free program removes known spyware which are mainly cookies.||||reg||1
Z||000011||SteveJ||10-30-2001||08:18 AM||||. . .and there is a free firewall that works very well called ZoneAlarm.  <A HREF="http://www.zonelabs.com/zap26_za_grid.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zonelabs.com/zap26_za_grid.html</A> <P>The base model zone arlarm is free and unlike some firewalls can be configured to prevent outgoing traffic such as a virus or spyware might do.||||reg||1
